   "The function hashes the raw calldata words with `calldatacopy(ptr, poolKey, 0xa0)` and does not mask each field to its declared width (address, uint24, int24). If a caller supplies a key whose padding bits are not clean, the result differs from `PoolIdLibrary.toId`, which hashes the cleaned, ABI-decoded values. This has no security effect here. The hook callbacks only receive keys that the PoolManager has encoded cleanly. The only other callers are `setPoolHookSwapFee`, which is owner-only, and `getPendingPositionRewards`, which is a view function, so a dirty key only harms the caller who sent it."
